</section></score></mdiv></body>
<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Thou great and good! Thou just and wise!</l><l>Hail! as our Father and our God!</l><l>For we are Thine by sacred ties,</l><l>Thy sons and daughters—bought with blood.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Then, Oh! to us this grace afford,</l><l>That far from Thee we ne’er may move;</l><l>Our guard—the presence of the Lord;</l><l>Our joy—Thy perfect present love.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>This gives us ever to rejoice,</l><l>Turning to light our darkest days;</l><l>And lifts on high each feeble voice,</l><l>While we have breath to pray or praise.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
